{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Do not turn to the idols.</b> To worship them; אֱלִילִים is a term of 'no' — as if it is worthless." "<b>And molten gods.</b> At the outset they are אֱלִילִים [mere nothings], and if you turn after them, you end up making them אֱלוֹהוּת [gods] (Sifra)." "<b>You shall not make for yourselves.</b> You shall not make for others, and others shall not make for you. And if you would say: I shall not make for myself, but others make for me — behold, it was already stated: ״לֹא יִהְיֶה לְךָ״ (Exodus 20) — neither yours nor another's."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:03.196186533Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}